golden_harness response bar for reference: 0.046 dB
   sweep bounded BY THE CONTRACT: HPF 20-1000 Hz, LPF 500-20000 Hz, Q 0.1-10.0  (defs/products/d24/dsp.csv)
   286 HPF/LPF sections, HPF 20-1000 Hz and LPF 500-20000 Hz, Q 0.1-10
   worst single-section |h|_1 = 13.80 (+22.8 dB) at ('hp', 20.0, 10.0)
   worst headroom bits: 1
   worst HPF+LPF CASCADE bound = 125.01 at HPF 521 Hz, LPF 500 Hz, Q 10  -> H = 4
   worst max|H| = 82.05 (+38.3 dB) at HPF 521 Hz, LPF 500 Hz, Q 10, peaking at 510 Hz
   -- what a PLAIN TONE reaches, against Q4.28's ceiling of 8.0
   through the round-once kernel, gate rectifier in front, 255.2 Hz sine (24000 samples):
     0 dBFS  H = 0: 205 internal wraps   -12 dBFS H = 0: 28   0 dBFS  H = 4 guarded: 0
   (the worst corner has the HPF ABOVE the LPF -- a setting nobody dials and a recalled preset can carry)
   *** H = 4 IS REACHABLE WITHIN THE CONTRACT, and it is not an adversarial sign pattern that gets there:
   max|H| over the same box is 82.1 (+38.3 dB) at 510 Hz, so a PLAIN TONE reaches it. The gate rectifies its
   key (r0 = abs r13) before the cascade, so a full-scale 255 Hz sine puts a 510 Hz component of 0.424 into
   the resonance: simulated through the round-once kernel that is 205 internal wraps in 24000 samples, and still
   28 at -12 dBFS. A wrap here is a sign inversion fed back into the poles of the level detector -- the
   gate slams on a loud signal. ***

   THE FIX, LANDED 2026-09-10: the gate sidechain's header word is INITIALISED to the contract worst H = 4
   (bq_h_load.GATE_SIDECHAIN_H, emitted by dsp_codegen into every _gate_filter_cq_* block). It cannot be sized at
   parameter load because the node has no parameter-load moment -- it converts every block and no swap-trigger cell
   says when the wire moved -- but its parameters ARE contract-bounded, so one constant covers every setting the
   wire can carry. In the INITIALISER, so it costs zero code bytes and zero instructions: the converter steps past the
   header and never writes it.
   the sweep's worst is H = 4 and the generator emits 4: COVERED.

   THE TALKBACK HPF IS NOT THE SAME CASE and is no longer counted with it. Its coefficient block has no entry in the
   SPI dispatch table -- the only talkback filter cell is Talk<nn>Hpf001, the ON/OFF word -- so the wire cannot
   reach it, it stays at its bypass initialiser, |h|_1 = 1 and H = 0 is correct.

   AND NONE OF IT REACHES A SHIPPING IMAGE. DSP4_BQ_FLOAT is the shipping cascade arm and it FORCES DSP4_BQ_GUARD off:
   the sidechain runs the 40-bit software float kernel, which has no fixed recursion to wrap. This section is the FIXED
   reference arm's bound -- the arm a future FPGA engine follows -- and that is where the fix lands.

4. WHAT ROUND-ONCE WOULD DELETE HERE, AND WHAT WOULD WRAP

   The dynamics path has no per-stage saturate of the biquad
   kind to delete. What it has is:
     _envq_fx        NO saturate at all, and correctly so --
                     fixed_ref.envelope_step's sat32 provably
                     never fires (section 1), so the asm
                     omitting it is an identity, not a
                     shortcut.
     _exp2q_fx       ONE saturate on the log2 -> linear
                     conversion, FEED-FORWARD. Deleting it
                     would wrap a large positive gain to a
                     NEGATIVE one -- a polarity inversion of
                     the whole strip -- and it is one
                     instruction on a branch that is already
                     there. There is nothing to win.
     _mrf_rns28[_simd]  the Q4.28 extract-and-saturate where
                     the gain is APPLIED. This is the GAIN
                     path's round-once question, priced
                     already (RIG C: 9.03 -> 3.55 c/sample/
                     strip, and the D20 mic-pre tap returns
                     the whole saving). It is feed-forward:
                     the wrap it would allow is a clipped
                     sample, not a state that rings on it.

   So the dynamics envelopes need NO guard, and the reason is
   not that they are gentle: it is that |h|_1 = 1 exactly for
   a one-pole smoother with a non-negative impulse response,
   against 378 for the worst biquad in the same design space.
   The per-cascade headroom pattern does not transfer because
   the hazard does not.

5. THE LEVEL -> GAIN TABLE FORM (DSP4_DYN_LUT), ceilings and
   saturation

   the LIMITER (slope 0x7FFFFFFF, hard knee) over its contract
   threshold range -30..0 dB: every word inside [0, 1] in
   Q4.28, largest 268435456 = 1.000000
   every table word over the documented parameter corners is
   inside [0, 1] in Q4.28; the largest seen is 268435456 = 1.000000
   the per-sample interpolation is a CONVEX COMBINATION of two
   such words, so its output is inside the same interval and
   cannot wrap. No guard word, no saturate, nothing to size.
   the multiply-and-round intermediate is under 2^59 in an
   80-bit MR, so it cannot overflow either.
   _exp2q_fx's saturate still runs -- ONCE PER TABLE POINT in
   the DESIGN step, not once per sample in the audio path.
   THE TABLE FORM DELETES A SATURATE FROM THE PER-SAMPLE PATH
   AND ADDS NONE.

   Interpolation ERROR is a different instrument and is not
   here: tools/dsp/dyn_lut_design.py measures it against
   fixed_ref directly (0.0950 dB worst over the documented
   sweep at K = 4, against PW's 0.1 dB bar; the LIMITER's own
   worst over its six contract thresholds is 0.0604 dB).


6. THE LINEAR-DOMAIN GATE THRESHOLD (DSP4_GATE_LINTHR)

   GateThr over the contract range -80 to 0 dB (0=-80/127=0/[Lin]), 801 points
   worst effective-threshold shift = +0.000320 dB at a threshold of -79.900 dB
   (the log arm opens at envelope 27155, the linear arm at 27154 -- ONE Q4.28 LSB apart)
   over any threshold at or above -60 dB: +0.000122 dB
   19 of 801 points exceed the documented 0.0002 dB, ALL of them at thresholds at or below -77.1 dB.
   The mechanism there is NOT the polynomials: at those thresholds the linear word itself is only a few tens of
   Q4.28 LSBs, so ONE LSB of quantisation is already worth more than the bar. The two arms are still one LSB apart.
